# Files ai-db must not index.
#
# Benchmark artifacts are generated data, not code. They are large, they change on
# every measurement run, and they contain the very words the golden queries search
# for: eval/results/token_budget.json is 63 KB of JSON full of "latency",
# "percentiles" and "telemetry", and indexing it put those words into the search
# space. A measurement must not be able to change the thing it measures.
#
# To be precise about what this does and does not fix: excluding it did NOT
# recover the retrieval baseline. recall@10 had already slid from 0.850 to 0.725
# before this file existed, purely from new test and benchmark source being
# added to a corpus whose eval root is ".". See the _note in eval/baseline.json
# for that bisect. This rule stops the generated data from making it worse.
eval/results/

# CI recreates this with `init --force`; it is a local artifact, not source.
ci.json

# Scratch output from ad-hoc runs.
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak
